Build the Windows debug configurations in CI

The debug option is only useful if something builds it. Unix targets
already carry debug and freethreaded+debug beside their optimised
options, so bring Windows into line: debug and freethreaded+debug on
x86_64 and i686, and debug on aarch64.

aarch64 gets the plain option only. Its free-threaded builds are newer
and less exercised than the x64 ones, and pairing a new configuration
with a new option is a poor way to learn which of the two failed.

windows-11-arm is also marked free, which it has been since the arm64
runners entered public preview. With free: false, find_runner cannot
match an aarch64 Windows runner and falls back to an x64 one, so these
builds cross-compile when a native runner is available.

diff --git a/ci-runners.yaml b/ci-runners.yaml
index e6bdd0f..b8740e6 100644
--- a/ci-runners.yaml
+++ b/ci-runners.yaml
@@ -45,7 +45,9 @@ windows-2025-vs2026:
   platform: windows
   free: true
 
+# Free for public repositories since the arm64 runners went into public
+# preview: https://github.com/orgs/community/discussions/155713
 windows-11-arm:
   arch: aarch64
   platform: windows
-  free: false
+  free: true
diff --git a/ci-targets.yaml b/ci-targets.yaml
index d75eb60..ec5db0f 100644
--- a/ci-targets.yaml
+++ b/ci-targets.yaml
@@ -387,9 +387,11 @@ windows:
       - "3.15"
     vs_version: "2022"
     build_options:
+      - debug
       - pgo
     build_options_conditional:
       - options:
+          - freethreaded+debug
           - freethreaded+pgo
         minimum-python-version: "3.13"
 
@@ -408,9 +410,11 @@ windows:
       vs_version: "2026"
       minimum-python-version: "3.15"
     build_options:
+      - debug
       - pgo
     build_options_conditional:
       - options:
+          - freethreaded+debug
           - freethreaded+pgo
         minimum-python-version: "3.13"
 
@@ -427,6 +431,7 @@ windows:
       - "3.15"
     vs_version: "2022"
     build_options:
+      - debug
       - pgo
     build_options_conditional:
       - options:
